{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider cannot run this dispute through POL-NS-04, because limb (b) fails on the chat log's own timestamps. Limb (a) is met — the rider's 07:22:10 message names his block — but the driver sent MSG-00205-002 ('ok coming') at 07:22:48, 38 seconds later and far inside the 120 second window, so no finding of unanswered rider contact can be entered against the driver and limb (c) is never reached. Disclosure of impairment, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires: EV-CHAT-00205 carries weight_multiplier 0.8 on issue CONTENT_REDACTED (the unit number in MSG-00205-001 was redacted). The redaction removes no timestamp and no sender, so the 38 second interval this claim rests on is untouched by the discount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00205", "EV-TRIP-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "The 4.00 fee cannot be carried by POL-NS-01, and the driver does not pretend otherwise. Limb (d) is excluded by the clause's own text because the trip terminated with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE; limb (b) fails because the driver's nearest approach to the pickup pin is 259.94 m against a 50 m STANDARD arrival radius; and limb (c) fails because the qualifying in-radius fix count is zero out of 92 driver fixes, leaving no in-geofence dwell to set against the 300 second minimum. This is exactly the case POL-NS-01 hands to POL-NS-03 — the category's clause for an honest mislocation rather than a manufactured no-show — and the dispute is to be reasoned there, not on the baseline clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00205", "EV-GPS-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "What the record does establish is an honest wrong-block attempt, and that distinction should be written into the ruling. The trip record computes a wait_time_min of 6.4 running from the arrived event at 07:26:40 to the cancellation at 07:33:05: the driver gave the rider six and a half minutes rather than harvesting a fee. His closest approach to the pin is 259.94 m — inside POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling and inside POL-NS-05's 300 m line. POL-NS-05 catches only an arrival fix that puts the driver more than 300 m out, or in motion at 15 kph or above, at the arrived timestamp; the published derived facts key no distance and no speed to that timestamp, and the only distance they publish sits inside the 300 m line, so the false-marker limb is not made out. This trip therefore belongs to the wrong-entrance route POL-NS-05's closing sentence preserves, and it should not be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00205", "EV-TRIP-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Two points are closed against the driver on this record and the driver does not stretch them. First, the pin-ambiguity limb of POL-NS-03(ii) requires trip_record.registered_pickup_points of 2 or more; this trip records one registered pickup point, so the platform-funded goodwill of 50 per cent — 2.00 against the 4.00 fee — is unavailable and the derived goodwill figure has nothing to attach to. Second, the rider did name the block, MSG-00205-001 reading 'im at blk 118', with the redaction removing only the unit number, so under POL-NS-03(i) the residual loss sits with the driver and no compensation is payable to him. The chat artifact is impaired at weight 0.8 on issue CONTENT_REDACTED, which is why the surviving block identifier, and not the redacted unit number, is the fact relied on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00205", "EV-CHAT-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "The sum charged is not open to attack on integrity grounds, and no partial refund can be built on it. The fare breakdown carries a single cancellation-fee line of 4.00 SGD, and 4.00 is exactly the greater of the two schedule figures this trip attracts — the STANDARD zone-class fee of 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of 4.00, the schedule dimension resolving to a tie — so the line reconciles with fee_schedule.resolution_rule and no limb of POL-NS-08(d) is engaged on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00205", "EV-TRIP-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.schedule_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no fee-farming pattern behind this cancelled trip. On the two fields POL-NS-07 names, and no others, driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the 4 the clause requires, and 2 over driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 104 is a rate of 0.019, below the 0.08 the clause also requires: the anti-farming test fails on both limbs, so nothing on the driver's 30-day record supports an adverse inference. On the rider side, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 against POL-NS-09(d)'s threshold of 3, and the counterparty-dispute counts are 0 and 0 against POL-NS-09(c)'s threshold of 2. Under POL-GEN-01 every other entry on either profile — rating, acceptance rate, lifetime counters — is context only and can ground nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00205", "EV-RPROF-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, and only if the Judge is not prepared to run the wrong-entrance findings, this case should be escalated rather than guessed at. The trip record and the trace contradict each other directly on arrival and dwell: the record enters an arrived event at 07:26:40 with a 6.4 minute wait, while the 92 driver fixes never come closer to the pin than 259.94 m and show zero in-geofence dwell. The published derived facts key neither a distance nor a speed to the arrived timestamp, so POL-NS-05 cannot be run (its condition needs a fix more than 300 m out or at 15 kph at that timestamp) and POL-NS-03 cannot be run either (its condition needs a stationary hold within 400 m). That head-on conflict between two admissible artifacts is what POL-NS-09(b) exists for, and under POL-GEN-03 the consequence is a terminal escalation with the disputed 4.00 held rather than refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00205", "EV-GPS-00205"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-05", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
